{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-125410" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/assets/82e3ae63881637f258ea92238bbcfc70f2e0993c17d74ce950d6457ffcd95039.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path along the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a73eff87a243f353549721bd5d900488a70f1f7bb2c99779b970432a261ecd7"} {"question" "q-125410" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/assets/d363cf00c4901fa0c29bb9521cdd2ea3c12c377dd8e38306df0d5a2837915a36.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. It's clear from the picture below that if we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/assets/c5799e631e7eb45ec5a9711ef1569d51b376d8c764a3226caa2676cdb968a6f5.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a73eff87a243f353549721bd5d900488a70f1f7bb2c99779b970432a261ecd7"} {"question" "q-125410" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a3071f644a35c8419b94dbbf157765a099d37438b76cbb14430473774f971160"} {"question" "q-125410" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a73eff87a243f353549721bd5d900488a70f1f7bb2c99779b970432a261ecd7"} {"question" "q-125410" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a73eff87a243f353549721bd5d900488a70f1f7bb2c99779b970432a261ecd7"} {"question" "q-125410" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a73eff87a243f353549721bd5d900488a70f1f7bb2c99779b970432a261ecd7"} {"question" "q-150011" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/assets/0d2aa60719643235f5ae684d59607199731626e15bac40fd6b14d071c099ab4a.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path along the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a73eff87a243f353549721bd5d900488a70f1f7bb2c99779b970432a261ecd7"} {"question" "q-150011" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$  works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/assets/2b8ef08638551571caa43150080a8550a0b61ed24eaa7c6da73fe66edd161e8e.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. It's clear from the picture below that if we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/assets/28db5c349d3455c58f81da7c181586ba4e0ad5662f35faa2575d6622b3713988.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a73eff87a243f353549721bd5d900488a70f1f7bb2c99779b970432a261ecd7"} {"question" "q-150011" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a3071f644a35c8419b94dbbf157765a099d37438b76cbb14430473774f971160"} {"question" "q-150011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a73eff87a243f353549721bd5d900488a70f1f7bb2c99779b970432a261ecd7"} {"question" "q-150011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a73eff87a243f353549721bd5d900488a70f1f7bb2c99779b970432a261ecd7"} {"question" "q-150011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a73eff87a243f353549721bd5d900488a70f1f7bb2c99779b970432a261ecd7"} {"question" "q-125706" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/assets/a423ab56220e438fb849d2025ab53b99bb74ef598e16110c911d691680130527.png)\n\nConsider the semicircle and constant vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be the path where the semicircle is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a73eff87a243f353549721bd5d900488a70f1f7bb2c99779b970432a261ecd7"} {"question" "q-125706" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statements I is false, while statement II is true. As the particle moves from $A$ to $B,$ the force $F$ works  against the particle for $x<0,$ while $F$  works with the particle for $x>0.$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/assets/cd52e91c72d481980c9a48575da7ca3eaebd2ed27f96b1054cf5c1c5da1aa3d9.png)\n\n \nBy symmetry, the contribution to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ for $x<0$ is canceled out by the contribution for $x>0.$ So, \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ is similar to the previous case.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/assets/a1e8fa5262fc787b691b3753fc57ab39aceee7c57dbbe166c6da6f6effaf42dc.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a73eff87a243f353549721bd5d900488a70f1f7bb2c99779b970432a261ecd7"} {"question" "q-125706" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a3071f644a35c8419b94dbbf157765a099d37438b76cbb14430473774f971160"} {"question" "q-125706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a73eff87a243f353549721bd5d900488a70f1f7bb2c99779b970432a261ecd7"} {"question" "q-125706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a73eff87a243f353549721bd5d900488a70f1f7bb2c99779b970432a261ecd7"} {"question" "q-125706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/1