icle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/assets/38868b69ae1836844a279e141d83b886f386c87edeedbb1e2067ffd18d7f1af3.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a73eff87a243f353549721bd5d900488a70f1f7bb2c99779b970432a261ecd7"} {"question" "q-125493" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a3071f644a35c8419b94dbbf157765a099d37438b76cbb14430473774f971160"} {"question" "q-125493" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a73eff87a243f353549721bd5d900488a70f1f7bb2c99779b970432a261ecd7"} {"question" "q-125493" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a73eff87a243f353549721bd5d900488a70f1f7bb2c99779b970432a261ecd7"} {"question" "q-125493" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a73eff87a243f353549721bd5d900488a70f1f7bb2c99779b970432a261ecd7"} {"question" "q-150018" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/assets/678ab825415e107bca9554d90e2ad5a4d8cc90a5ef68d817972ef98dfc165922.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path along the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a73eff87a243f353549721bd5d900488a70f1f7bb2c99779b970432a261ecd7"} {"question" "q-150018" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion  of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. Since the force $F$ acts perpendicular to the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B,$ it neither helps nor hinders its motion. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/assets/0e8d0fcf619987f49869cc6ae9eb5cb0c7acbbb23f45ce8f64626dfd1debdc63.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ is similar to the previous case.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/assets/b2bec1f1da172b623f20d28fd0e9c5a248cf00dc621769851ca33b3b545b8592.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a73eff87a243f353549721bd5d900488a70f1f7bb2c99779b970432a261ecd7"} {"question" "q-150018" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a3071f644a35c8419b94dbbf157765a099d37438b76cbb14430473774f971160"} {"question" "q-150018" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a73eff87a243f353549721bd5d900488a70f1f7bb2c99779b970432a261ecd7"} {"question" "q-150018" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a73eff87a243f353549721bd5d900488a70f1f7bb2c99779b970432a261ecd7"} {"question" "q-150018" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a73eff87a243f353549721bd5d900488a70f1f7bb2c99