5458d68deabda91f56bf63e7c8f59f5ea79c68292332d8cd58d4f.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a73eff87a243f353549721bd5d900488a70f1f7bb2c99779b970432a261ecd7"} {"question" "q-125380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a3071f644a35c8419b94dbbf157765a099d37438b76cbb14430473774f971160"} {"question" "q-125380" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a73eff87a243f353549721bd5d900488a70f1f7bb2c99779b970432a261ecd7"} {"question" "q-125380" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a73eff87a243f353549721bd5d900488a70f1f7bb2c99779b970432a261ecd7"} {"question" "q-125380" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a73eff87a243f353549721bd5d900488a70f1f7bb2c99779b970432a261ecd7"} {"question" "e-9536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/assets/d51d0cea4b75dffe5eef6ccf46e5156716eb1381d20b4193d811acfe83278094.png)\n\n \n\nConsider the curve and constant vector field $\\mathbf F$ shown above. Let $C$ be the path where the curve is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r > 0$\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r =                 0$\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r =  0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/example-9536.json" "file_sha256" "1e7ff2d0465013f387171847105aa574af2e0750b0f9f3f4c3eff5ad44e5d59a"} {"question" "e-9536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r$ gives the total work done by a force $\\mathbf F$ in moving a particle along $C\\mathbin{:}$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r > 0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r <                                 0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statements I is false, while statement II is true. As the particle moves from $A$ to $B,$ the force $\\mathbf F$ works with the particle for $x >        0,$ while $\\mathbf F$  works against the particle for $x <           0.$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/assets/673798bb131da05a07b3f47894340cbbc143fa6a248823bcfbdf6b5a5238efb4.png)\n\n \nBy symmetry, the contribution to $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r$ for $x <                 0$ is canceled out by the contribution for $x > 0.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r =     0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $\\mathbf F$ is similar to the previous case.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/assets/24884d31b2b9aa8d94b11bccfaab1fa31e62a34f4e5183676c79390923f1f243.png)\n\n \nSo, $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r =      0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/example-9536.json" "file_sha256" "1e7ff2d0465013f387171847105aa574af2e0750b0f9f3f4c3eff5ad44e5d59a"} {"question" "e-9542" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/assets/298b7b4293ff104a62107670fa2aba603b8a23e9ad042f7e270a4acf6267a2fa.png)\n\n \n\nConsider the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y)$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path where the curve is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r <  0$\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r =         0$\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r >  0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058183/example-9542.json" "file_sha256" "1a834f9e0722aa63751ab7f73343572360eef5297ed772756eb627a5b84b09c8"} {"question" "e-9542" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textr